          "english_quote": "Does not what seems to be done evilly bring delight to the doer but punishment to the sufferer?",
          "issue": "“Does not” frames the question as expecting agreement. That is contextually defensible within Simon’s argument, but μήτιγε ordinarily carries a doubtful or negative expectation. Unlike the other difficult constructions here, this consequential choice of rhetorical force is not disclosed.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note explaining why the argument supports the affirmative-leaning English question and preserving the doubtful alternative, such as “Is it really the case that what seems to be done evilly delights the doer but punishes the sufferer?” Alternatively, propose a less leading main question with that explanation. The revised wording or note requires fresh review; no Greek emendation or print verification is needed.",
